{
  "_doc": "BOATZ workshop art — mutable industrial building icons drawn on an island by the engine's generic `drawUnifiedArt` (same schema as data/ship-art.json). Coordinates are radius-relative (multiplied by `r` at render time) unless marked `Abs`; UP is -y, the ground baseline sits near +0.6, and these icons are NOT rotated by the renderer (unlike ships) so they draw upright. TOP-LEVEL container key is `workshops`, keyed by the FOUR industrial goods — `Weapons` (gun-foundry / forge), `Clothing` (weaver's / dye workshop), `LuxuryGoods` (jeweller's atelier), `Ships` (shipwright's slipway). Register it to MATCH the container key so buildArtRegistry unwraps it, e.g. `buildArtRegistry({ workshops: workshopArt })` → `art.workshops.Weapons`; a mismatched key leaves the whole object (incl this _doc) as the registry. Each good defines THREE `states`: `running` (healthy, staffed, working — full ink, upright, saturated fills, motif present, live forge/glint + a rising chimney smoke plume), `idle` (unstaffed / unfunded / input-starved — the SAME intact silhouette but muted & ghosted via lowered alpha + greyed fills, motif cold, no smoke), and `disrepair` (derelict, condition ~0 — a BROKEN SILHOUETTE: the intact roof/structure shapes are swapped out via `visibleStates` for a caved/jagged/collapsed roof + rubble, so the state reads by SHAPE not just tint for colour-blind viewers, motif gone, no smoke). State geometry swaps are done with `visibleStates` (checked for any shape in shapes.js) rather than per-state `points` overrides, so no mismatched-length point arrays are lerped during a transition. The chimney/forge SMOKE is authored in-file as a `running`-only `group` (`visibleStates:[\"running\"]`) of cheap filled `circle` puffs animated on the ambient `*` clip (rise + grow + fade); it deliberately does NOT reference the vfx `damageSmoke` effect nor use `createRadialGradient` — hundreds of these can be on-screen at once, so it is plain filled arcs + alpha only. All shapes set explicit fill/stroke colours, so the icons render as a fixed ink-on-parchment palette regardless of the base `color` passed to drawUnifiedArt (no faction tint by design).",

